Description:

Formula described by Buddhi at the Forums;

http://www.fractalforums.com/the-3d-mandelbulb/new-mandelbulb-like-formulas/

Extended version; thousands of variants possible.

Depending on the options the fractal can become too noisy or very distorted,
to remedy try to enable the NoYZ/R^3 option;

If NoYZ/R^3 = 1 -> You disable YZ rotation altogether.
The second slider stops to work, and the fractal usually tends to be less fuzzy.
The formula is very different though.
If NoYZ/R^3 = 2 -> Multiplying by R^2 (instead by R), it tends to smooth out the
fractal a little, but don't ask me about mathematical correctness :D
If NoYZ/R^3 = 3 -> Both of the above (well, the result is not so good but you choose).